# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GrillSearch environment
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. (DATABASE_URL lives in `.env`, not here.)
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Serper API key — Google Search JSON API used to query automotive forums.
# Get one at https://serper.dev. WITHOUT this key the app runs in demo mode
# (clearly-labeled sample forum threads), so the full pipeline + AI synthesis
# still work end-to-end for local development.
SERPER_API_KEY=

# ── LLM auth: NO key required by default ────────────────────────────────────
# Claude synthesis runs via the Claude Agent SDK (@anthropic-ai/claude-agent-sdk),
# which inherits this machine's existing Claude Code login (the OAuth credentials
# in ~/.claude/.credentials.json — run `claude` once to authenticate). So on a
# host that already has Claude Code logged in, you do NOT set any LLM key here.
#
# OPTIONAL OVERRIDES (only if you are NOT relying on the inherited Claude Code
# login — e.g. serving other users, or a headless host):
#   - ANTHROPIC_API_KEY        usage-billed API key (recommended for multi-user)
#   - CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN  long-lived subscription token from `claude setup-token`
# If either is present in the environment, the Agent SDK uses it automatically.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=
